{"id":"mahabharata-13-049","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":49,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 49 · The sons of each order","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks Bhishma to name the sons of each order separately, by which women and by whom. Bhishma tells of the Magadha and the Vamaka, the sons of vaishyas by brahmin and kshatriya women, and of the kinds of adopted and made sons, and ends by saying that this is the rule of the orders in the books of dharma.","kn":"ಪ್ರತಿ ವರ್ಣದ ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಯಾವ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರಿಂದ, ಯಾರಿಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದವರೆಂದು ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕ ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವೈಶ್ಯನಿಗೆ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣಿ-ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯೆಯರಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಮಾಗಧ, ವಾಮಕರನ್ನು, ದತ್ತಕ ಮತ್ತು ಕೃತಕ ಪುತ್ರರ ವಿಧಗಳನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर प्रत्येक वर्ण के पुत्रों को अलग-अलग, किन स्त्रियों से और किससे, बताने को कहते हैं। भीष्म वैश्य के ब्राह्मणी और क्षत्रिया से हुए मागध और वामक का वर्णन करते हैं, गोद और बनाए पुत्रों के भेद बताते हैं और कहते हैं कि यह धर्मशास्त्रों में वर्णों का निश्चय है।","te":"ప్రతి వర్ణం కొడుకులను, ఏ స్త్రీల నుండి, ఎవరికి అని వేర్వేరుగా చెప్పమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. వైశ్యునికి బ్రాహ్మణి, క్షత్రియ స్త్రీల నుండి కలిగిన మాగధ, వామకులను, దత్త, కృతక పుత్రుల రకాలను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"ஒவ்வொரு வருணத்தின் மக்களையும் எந்தப் பெண்களிடம் யாருக்குப் பிறந்தவர் என்று தனித்தனியாகக் கூறுமாறு யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, வைசியனுக்கு அந்தணி, க்ஷத்திரியப் பெண்களிடம் பிறந்த மாகதர், வாமகர் மற்றும் தத்து, செயற்கை மகன்களின் வகைகளைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ഓരോ വർണ്ണത്തിലെയും പുത്രന്മാരെ, ഏതു സ്ത്രീകളിൽനിന്ന്, ആരാൽ ജനിച്ചവരെന്ന് വെവ്വേറെ പറയണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. വൈശ്യരുടെ പുത്രന്മാരായ മാഗധന്മാരെയും വാമകന്മാരെയും, അവർ ബ്രാഹ്മണ, ക്ഷത്രിയ സ്ത്രീകളിൽ ജനിച്ചവരാണെന്നും, ദത്തുപുത്രന്മാരുടെയും നിർമ്മിച്ച പുത്രന്മാരുടെയും തരങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ധർമ്മശാസ്ത്രങ്ങളിലെ വർണ്ണനിയമം ഇതാണെന്ന് പറഞ്ഞ് അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.49; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ब्रूहि पुत्रान्कुरुश्रेष्ठ वर्णानां त्वं पृथक्पृथक् ।\nकीदृश्यां कीदृशाश्चापि पुत्राः कस्य च के च ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Kurus, tell me about the sons of each class, one by one: of what kind of woman, what kind of sons, whose they are, and who they are."}},{"n":2,"text":"विप्रवादाः सुबहुशः श्रूयन्ते पुत्रकारिताः ।\nअत्र नो मुह्यतां राजन्संशयं छेत्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Very many conflicting views about sons are heard. Since we are confused about this, king, you should cut our doubt."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"आत्मा पुत्रस्तु विज्ञेयस्तस्यानन्तरजश्च यः ।\nनियुक्तजश्च विज्ञेयः सुतः प्रसृतजस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of one's own self is to be known, and the one born next after him, the one born by appointment, and the one born of a woman who moved away."}},{"n":4,"text":"पतितस्य च भार्यायां भर्त्रा सुसमवेतया ।\nतथा दत्तकृतौ पुत्रावध्यूढश्च तथापरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Also the son of a fallen man's wife, begotten with her husband's agreement, the two adopted sons, the given and the made, and another, the one taken over after the mother's marriage."}},{"n":5,"text":"षडपध्वंसजाश्चापि कानीनापसदास्तथा ।\nइत्येते ते समाख्यातास्तान्विजानीहि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are also the six born of a degradation, and the kanina and the apasada. These have been named for you, Bharata; know them."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"षडपध्वंसजाः के स्युः के वाप्यपसदास्तथा ।\nएतत्सर्वं यथातत्त्वं व्याख्यातुं मे त्वमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who are the six born of degradation, and who are the apasadas? You should explain all this truly to me."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"त्रिषु वर्णेषु ये पुत्रा ब्राह्मणस्य युधिष्ठिर ।\nवर्णयोश्च द्वयोः स्यातां यौ राजन्यस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, a brahmin's sons in three classes, and the two a kshatriya's in two classes, Bharata,"}},{"n":8,"text":"एको द्विवर्ण एवाथ तथात्रैवोपलक्षितः ।\nषडपध्वंसजास्ते हि तथैवापसदाञ्शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"and one of two classes: these are marked out here as the six born of degradation. Now hear also the apasadas."}},{"n":9,"text":"चण्डालो व्रात्यवेनौ च ब्राह्मण्यां क्षत्रियासु च ।\nवैश्यायां चैव शूद्रस्य लक्ष्यन्तेऽपसदास्त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Chandala, the Vratya and the Vena, born of a brahmin woman, a kshatriya woman and a vaishya woman to a shudra, are marked as three apasadas."}},{"n":10,"text":"मागधो वामकश्चैव द्वौ वैश्यस्योपलक्षितौ ।\nब्राह्मण्यां क्षत्रियायां च क्षत्रियस्यैक एव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Magadha and the Vamaka are the two marked for a vaishya, by a brahmin woman and a kshatriya woman; for a kshatriya there is only one."}},{"n":11,"text":"ब्राह्मण्यां लक्ष्यते सूत इत्येतेऽपसदाः स्मृताः ।\nपुत्ररेतो न शक्यं हि मिथ्या कर्तुं नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Suta born of a brahmin woman is marked. These are remembered as apasadas. For seed that has produced a son cannot be made false, lord of men."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"क्षेत्रजं केचिदेवाहुः सुतं केचित्तु शुक्रजम् ।\nतुल्यावेतौ सुतौ कस्य तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some say the field-born son is the son, others the one born of seed. Whose is each of these two sons, being equal? Tell me, grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"रेतजो वा भवेत्पुत्रस्त्यक्तो वा क्षेत्रजो भवेत् ।\nअध्यूढः समयं भित्त्वेत्येतदेव निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A son may be born of seed, or a son born in the field may be cast off, or one who is taken over, breaking an agreement. Learn this from me."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"रेतोजं विद्म वै पुत्रं क्षेत्रजस्यागमः कथम् ।\nअध्यूढं विद्म वै पुत्रं हित्वा च समयं कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We know the son born of seed, but how does the field-born son come? And how do we know the taken-over son, who has left the agreement?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"आत्मजं पुत्रमुत्पाद्य यस्त्यजेत्कारणान्तरे ।\nन तत्र कारणं रेतः स क्षेत्रस्वामिनो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If a man who has fathered a son of his own body casts him off for some other reason, the seed is not the cause there; the son would belong to the owner of the field."}},{"n":16,"text":"पुत्रकामो हि पुत्रार्थे यां वृणीते विशां पते ।\nतत्र क्षेत्रं प्रमाणं स्यान्न वै तत्रात्मजः सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, when a man who wants a son chooses a woman for the sake of a son, the field is the authority there, and not the son of his own body."}},{"n":17,"text":"अन्यत्र क्षेत्रजः पुत्रो लक्ष्यते भरतर्षभ ।\nन ह्यात्मा शक्यते हन्तुं दृष्टान्तोपगतो ह्यसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elsewhere, bull of the Bharatas, a field-born son is recognized; for the self cannot be killed, and he has come under the illustration."}},{"n":18,"text":"कश्चिच्च कृतकः पुत्रः संग्रहादेव लक्ष्यते ।\nन तत्र रेतः क्षेत्रं वा प्रमाणं स्याद्युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"A certain son by adoption is recognized only through acceptance. Yudhishthira, neither seed nor field is the authority there."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"कीदृशः कृतकः पुत्रः संग्रहादेव लक्ष्यते ।\nशुक्रं क्षेत्रं प्रमाणं वा यत्र लक्ष्येत भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"What kind of adopted son is recognized only through acceptance, Bharata, where neither seed, field nor authority is looked to?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"मातापितृभ्यां संत्यक्तं पथि यं तु प्रलक्षयेत् ।\nन चास्य मातापितरौ ज्ञायेते स हि कृत्रिमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is found on the road, abandoned by his mother and father, and whose parents are not known, is the adopted one."}},{"n":21,"text":"अस्वामिकस्य स्वामित्वं यस्मिन्संप्रतिलक्षयेत् ।\nसवर्णस्तं च पोषेत सवर्णस्तस्य जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One in whom a man finds lordship over one who has no master, being of the same class, should raise him, and he is born as his own of the same class."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"कथमस्य प्रयोक्तव्यः संस्कारः कस्य वा कथम् ।\nदेया कन्या कथं चेति तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"How should the rite of purification be done for him, and by whom, and how should a daughter be given? Tell me that, grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"आत्मवत्तस्य कुर्वीत संस्कारं स्वामिवत्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should perform the rite for him as for himself, and as an owner."}},{"n":24,"text":"त्यक्तो मातापितृभ्यां यः सवर्णं प्रतिपद्यते ।\nतद्गोत्रवर्णतस्तस्य कुर्यात्संस्कारमच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who is abandoned by mother and father and is taken in by one of his own class, unfailing one, the rite should be done according to the gotra and class of that man."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथ देया तु कन्या स्यात्तद्वर्णेन युधिष्ठिर ।\nसंस्कर्तुं मातृगोत्रं च मातृवर्णविनिश्चये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, a daughter would be given according to his class; and the rite is to be done, with the mother's gotra, when the mother's class is determined."}},{"n":26,"text":"कानीनाध्यूढजौ चापि विज्ञेयौ पुत्रकिल्बिषौ ।\nतावपि स्वाविव सुतौ संस्कार्याविति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kanina and the adhyudhaja are known as sons with a fault; yet it is settled that they too are to be purified like his own sons."}},{"n":27,"text":"क्षेत्रजो वाप्यपसदो येऽध्यूढास्तेषु चाप्यथ ।\nआत्मवद्वै प्रयुञ्जीरन्संस्कारं ब्राह्मणादयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the field-born, the apasada and the adhyudha sons, brahmins and others should perform the rite as for their own."}},{"n":28,"text":"धर्मशास्त्रेषु वर्णानां निश्चयोऽयं प्रदृश्यते ।\nएतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं किं भूयः श्रोतुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the settlement of the classes seen in the dharma treatises. I have told you all this. What more do you wish to hear?"}}]}]}